# Redmi K70 (vermeer) kernel configuration. CONFIG_XNU_<NAME> maps to XNU_<NAME>.
# arch:configs/common.config (arm64e) already sets BUILD_ARCHIVES, SOURCE_CORECRYPTO14,
# SOURCE_PTHREAD, ARM_DT_PLATFORM, ARMCPU, NATIVE_ARCH_TIMER and NATIVE_PAN.
CONFIG_XNU_ARMVIRT_PLATFORM=n
# The OS profile's ipados.config selects "prelinked", which leaves the original corecrypto as
# the only provider: build-xnu-4k-baseline.sh then undefines XNU_SOURCE_CORECRYPTO14 for
# prng_random.o. OSKext.cpp keeps the define, so its calls to source_corecrypto14_original and
# source_corecrypto14_start_once stay and the first pass fails to link, because that pass
# links no crypto archive:
#   Undefined symbols for architecture arm64e:
#     "_source_corecrypto14_original", referenced from OSKext::start(bool)
# "source" keeps the definitions in prng_random.o and is what UniXNU-sheng selects for the same
# ipados-27.0.1-24A446 profile.
CONFIG_XNU_CRYPTO_BOOTSTRAP="source"
# The prelink emits an MH_FILESET kernel and the kit's fileset_layout.split_references reads the
# linker's LC_DYLD_CHAINED_FIXUPS (v2 split-segment records). Without this switch the linked
# kernel has no such command and the prelink stops with "Native image has no split-segment
# relocation information". UniXNU-sheng enables it for the same profile.
CONFIG_XNU_KERNEL_CHAINED_FIXUPS=y
# soc:configs/sm8550.config sets CONFIG_XNU_NATIVE_ADRENO=y. It is turned off here until the
# board's GPU inputs exist (ZAP firmware, GMU votes, GPU SMMU windows): Adreno740/AdrenoMetal
# are not in [components] and their archives are not in [kernel] archives, so the kernel must
# not reference them. Re-enable the flag, both components and their archive entries together.
# CONFIG_XNU_NATIVE_ADRENO is not set
# Storage is on. The UFS driver is not a standalone kext on arm64e: build-arm-driver.py routes
# ShengUfs to build-sheng-source-storage.py, which builds the deferred IOBlockStorageDevice
# adapter plus the SourceStorage runtime that loads the original IOStorageFamily and APFS and
# authenticates the signed root policies. That makes the policy bundle a build input, so
# scripts/policies/ipados-27.0.1-24A446 carries the OS and SystemOS headers and their 395-byte
# owner anchor. Those are the same files sheng uses for this profile, and they are the right
# ones because the profile pins the same image: os_image_sha256 8a12cdad... and
# systemos_image_sha256 d5b4873d... with the matching volume UUIDs.
#
# CONFIG_XNU_NATIVE_UFS must stay OFF here, unlike sheng's iPadOS 17 base config. It does two
# things at once: it force-loads build/sheng-ufs/libShengUfs.a (line 641 of
# build-xnu-4k-baseline.sh) and it defines XNU_NATIVE_UFS for the personality table
# (native-aes-personality.patch), which publishes NativeUfs personalities against
# IOPlatformDevice and IOPlatformExpertDevice. In the source-storage design the class registers
# late - SourceStorage's preModLoad runs the deferred constructors after IOStorageFamily loads,
# long after IOKit has matched personalities - so every matching provider node logs
# 'Couldn't alloc class "NativeUfs"' (36 of them on the first boot) and any provider that
# matches after registration could start a second, unmanaged instance. sheng's
# sheng_ipados27_defconfig for this same profile does not set it either. The archive still has
# to reach the link, which CONFIG_XNU_EXTRA_LD_ARCHIVES below does the way sheng does it.
#
# CONFIG_XNU_SOURCE_STORAGE_TABLES="userdata" keeps only the 544-byte signed header in the boot
# image and leaves the block tables in the userdata image, which is what lets the payload stay
# inside the fastboot size limit.
CONFIG_XNU_SOURCE_STORAGE=y
CONFIG_XNU_SOURCE_STORAGE_TABLES="userdata"
CONFIG_XNU_EXTRA_LD_ARCHIVES="-Wl,-force_load,{tree}/build/sheng-source-storage/libShengSourceStorage.a"
# The mount gate needs the owner verdict. bsd_init's FSIOC_KERNEL_ROOTAUTH seal check fails on
# a source-built root, and offline-owner-root-binding-audit.patch tolerates that failure only
# through the owner verdict: the root mounted read-only AND native_verified_block_root_authorized()
# on the mounted device (SourceRootBinding.cpp's IOMedia walk into the verified UFS window). The
# third boot proved everything before it - transport, GPT, manifest, policy authentication, window
# verification, publication and the mount itself - and then panicked at that gate. sheng-27 sets
# both flags for this profile; the baseline's own validation accepts them with XNU_SOURCE_STORAGE=y.
# The Data-volume, cache-mount and SystemOS-union members of the family stay off: each needs a
# Data seed this board does not carry yet.
CONFIG_XNU_OWNER_ROOT_AUDIT=y
CONFIG_XNU_OWNER_ROOT_TRUST=y
